==English==

===Etymology===
From {{confix|en|mono|gamous}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/məˈnɒɡəməs/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/məˈnɑɡəməs/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-monogamous.wav|a=UK}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|narrowly}} Being [[married]] to one person at a time.
# {{lb|en|broadly}} Being [[exclusive]]ly [[committed]] to one [[significant other]] at a time.
# {{lb|en|zoology}} Having only one [[sexual]] [[partner]] at a time.
# {{lb|en|botany}} [[monogamic|Monogamic]]; having a simple flower with united [[anther]]s.

